# macOS title-bar clicks

On macOS, Jcat's title bar must not swallow clicks. This has regressed more than once: Settings, More, the language menu, Run, Compile, and the run-class menu stop opening.

Cause: `-webkit-app-region: drag` anywhere in the window. With `titleBarStyle: 'hiddenInset'`, a drag region steals real mouse clicks. A `no-drag` child inside a drag parent is not enough. A transparent control is also not enough: macOS ignores it and drags the window. DevTools and synthesized clicks bypass that hit test and hide the bug.

Rules:

- Do not set `-webkit-app-region: drag` or `app-region: drag` on any element. `html`, `body`, and the title bar stay `no-drag`.
- The macOS window uses `titleBarStyle: 'hidden'`, not `hiddenInset`. `hiddenInset` leaves a dead strip where the window title would be, and Settings clicks never arrive there. Traffic lights stay positioned with `trafficLightPosition`.
- Move the window from the title bar's pointer handler. Skip buttons, menus, and inputs. A 4px threshold keeps a click from becoming a drag.
- Double-click on empty title-bar space toggles zoom, including on macOS.
- `.actions` and `.title-end` keep an opaque `background-color` (`var(--paper)`).
- Every title-bar button, including Settings, keeps an opaque `background-color`.
- A closing dialog must not leave `.modal-backdrop` on screen. While it is leaving (`is-out`), it has `pointer-events: none`.
- After any title-bar or dialog change, verify a real pointer click opens Settings. Do not treat a DevTools click as proof.

Dropdowns (language, More, run class, sort) open with a clip animation. `grid-template-rows: auto` does not interpolate, so the menu appears all at once. `1fr` collapses on an absolutely positioned menu. Keep `clip-path: inset(...)`.
